Z||000000||BAM-BAM||02-03-2001||11:39 PM||||  Went to the yard today and found a complete set of gauges including the aux gauges for $50.00. My question is where do the aux gauges plug in. Should I have gotten a different connector or something? It's a nice set too. Cleaned up to almost perfect condition. And would you belive the the odometer read within 7/10th's of mine. How's that for amazing!!!! I want to install then asap. Also, I dont have the correct radio pod console, can the coupe console be used with the aux gauges? LMK,TIA<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||02-04-2001||12:47 AM||||The good news is that the 120 MPH speedo is a simple bolt on thing.....just remove the old 85 MPH one and reinstal the 120.<P>The bad news is that since the aux. gauges weren't available until '86 it isn't a simple plug & play.  You'll have to find the right wires that go to the oil & volt gauges and splice into them  to get the aux. gauges to work.<P>You might be able to cut the solid pod to get the gauges fit, but it won't look right.  You're best bet is to find the proper pod and install it.<BR>||||reg||1
